tus", "url": "https://x.com/plainionist/status/2093402227599687718", "id": "2093402227599687718", "text": "\"I did not become a programmer because of a deep love of if statements.\n\nI became a programmer because I wanted programs.\n\nI wanted things to exist that did not exist.\" -- @dhh", "raw_text": {"text": "\"I did not become a programmer because of a deep love of if statements.\n\nI became a programmer because I wanted programs.\n\nI wanted things to exist that did not exist.\" -- @dhh", "display_text_range": [0, 176], "facets": [{"type": "mention", "indices": [172, 176], "original": "dhh", "id": "14561327"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "plainionist", "url": "https://x.com/plainionist", "id": "962440906753363968", "followers": 1847, "following": 400, "likes": 11094, "media_count": 361, "statuses": 7348, "name": "Seb", "description": "25+ yrs battle-tested Software Engineering | Architecture, Clean Code, AI in dev | Hot takes + Deep dives | YouTube insights \ud83d\udc47| Let's discuss! \ud83d\ude80", "raw_description": {"text": "25+ yrs battle-tested Software Engineering | Architecture, Clean Code, AI in dev | Hot takes + Deep dives | YouTube insights \ud83d\udc47| Let's discuss! \ud83d\ude80", "facets": []}, "location": "Lost in Code", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/962440906753363968/1772514416", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1660289602790342658/PYgGb9zX_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Sat Feb 10 21:39:28 +0000 2018", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://youtube.com/@AboutCleanCode", "display_url": "youtube.com/@AboutCleanCode"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 28, "reposts": 36, "likes": 342, "bookmarks": 34, "quotes": 6, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri Aug 28 18:15:59 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787940959, "views": 20690, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": {"id": "9505092", "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin"}}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2093408489653583903", "id": "2093408489653583903", "text": "Why is the coverage if the dispatcher so low?\n>Because it spawns processes that the coverage tool can't see.\nAre those processes tested by themselves?\n>Yes.\nCan you mock the spawning and just test the dispatching?\n>Yes.\nThen do that.\n>Coverage is now 100%\nThank you. (sigh).", "raw_text": {"text": "Why is the coverage if the dispatcher so low?\n&gt;Because it spawns processes that the coverage tool can't see.\nAre those processes tested by themselves?\n&gt;Yes.\nCan you mock the spawning and just test the dispatching?\n&gt;Yes.\nThen do that.\n&gt;Coverage is now 100%\nThank you. (sigh).", "display_text_range": [0, 286], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 3, "reposts": 1, "likes": 64, "bookmarks": 12, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri Aug 28 18:40:52 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787942452, "views": 13823, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2093314633939476920", "id": "2093314633939476920", "text": "Rights.  What are they?  If something is a right, then it MUST be provided.  If we assert that healthcare is a right, then we MUST provide it -- by force if necessary. \n\nWhat force would be necessary?  Taxation would, of course, be the first force to be applied.  But taxation is not sufficient.  We'd also have to force providers.  We could not allow providers to set their fees, schedules, or even their careers.  We would HAVE to guarantee that there would be enough providers, of the right kinds, and in the right places, at all times.  So we'd have to force the people with aptitude to become providers, and deprive them of any options.  We'd have to make it illegal for those who are able to provide, to refuse to provide.\n\nSome governments claim that they offer healthcare as a right.  But they don't.  What they offer instead is a queue to access a scarce resource.  Worse, that queue is not served by the best -- because the best go where they can be paid what they are worth.", "raw_text": {"text": "Rights.  What are they?  If something is a right, then it MUST be provided.  If we assert that healthcare is a right, then we MUST provide it -- by force if necessary. \n\nWhat force would be necessary?  Taxation would, of course, be the first force to be applied.  But taxation is not sufficient.  We'd also have to force providers.  We could not allow providers to set their fees, schedules, or even their careers.  We would HAVE to guarantee that there would be enough providers, of the right kinds, and in the right places, at all times.  So we'd have to force the people with aptitude to become providers, and deprive them of any options.  We'd have to make it illegal for those who are able to provide, to refuse to provide.\n\nSome governments claim that they offer healthcare as a right.  But they don't.  What they offer instead is a queue to access a scarce resource.  Worse, that queue is not served by the best -- because the best go where they can be paid what they are worth.", "display_text_range": [0, 985], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 84, "reposts": 27, "likes": 479, "bookmarks": 66, "quotes": 4, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri Aug 28 12:27:55 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787920075, "views": 32256, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2092632165968121921", "id": "2092632165968121921", "text": "What a fascinating reversal.  We are now using code to constrain reasoning agents.  We used to be reasoning agents that constrained code.", "raw_text": {"text": "What a fascinating reversal.  We are now using code to constrain reasoning agents.  We used to be reasoning agents that constrained code.", "display_text_range": [0, 137], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followe